{
  "Name": "Okta - Admin & Configuration Changes - Unauthorized Scope for Public App OAuth2 Token Grant with Client Credentials",
  "Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Admin & Configuration Changes\nMITRE ATT&CK: Defense Evasion / T1550.001\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Unauthorized Scope for Public App OAuth2 Token Grant with Client Credentials\" or \"<ip>|Unauthorized Scope for Public App OAuth2 Token Grant with Client Credentials\"\n\nOAuth 2.0 client-credentials token requests (app.oauth2.token.grant / app.oauth2.as.token.grant) that fail with no_matching_scope: an app asked for a scope it has not been granted. A stolen client secret is often probed for broader scopes this way.\n\nFalse positives: a misconfigured integration after a scope change.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/defense_evasion_first_occurence_public_app_client_credential_token_exchange/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/defense_evasion_first_occurence_public_app_client_credential_token_exchange.toml",
  "Labels": [
    "okta",
    "detection",
    "admin-configuration-changes",
    "defense-evasion",
    "T1550.001"
  ],
  "Schedule": "7,22,37,52 * * * *",
  "Duration": -900,
  "DefaultDeploymentRules": {
    "Disabled": false,
    "RunImmediately": false
  },
